<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  Upstream ships `aps-environment: development` here, but this app
  registers for NO remote notifications: there is no
  registerForRemoteNotifications, no didRegisterForRemoteNotificationsWith…,
  no UNUserNotificationCenter delegate and no push SDK anywhere in
  ios/*.swift, app/, screens/ or ui/ — the only notification dependency is
  @notifee/react-native, which schedules LOCAL reminders.

  An entitlement the App ID does not carry makes the provisioning profile
  refuse the signature, so an unused `aps-environment` would break the very
  first TestFlight upload; and the privacy policy says the app sends no
  push. Both reasons point the same way, so the entitlement is removed
  rather than the Push Notifications capability enabled on the App ID.

  The matching `remote-notification` background mode is removed from
  Info.plist for the same reason. `fetch` and `processing` stay: they are
  what continues wallet synchronisation.

  If a real push feature is ever added, put `aps-environment` back AND
  enable Push Notifications on the `green.swarm.swarmwallet` App ID.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
